From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm5: fuse routed moe_sum with the shared-expert add

VLLM_GLM5_MOE_SUM_ADD (default 0; read once per process). MoERunner.forward
arms a host-side hand-off around its experts call (decode: M <= 32, bf16,
shared experts present, no routed scale/transform/padding/reduction/dispatch
between experts and the add). The compiled Marlin decode then leaves its
c3 [M,8,K] unsummed and the runner computes
    bf16(f32(shared) + f32(bf16(sum_k f32(c3[:,k]))))
in one Triton launch (port of Morrowmake idx_glue._moe_sum_add_kernel)
instead of moe_sum + an elementwise bf16 add. Same slot order and rounding
points: bit-identical. Any other MoE path is unchanged; an offer that cannot
be fused is flushed with ops.moe_sum exactly as before.

